  The URLs here, the <link rel="canonical"> in each page and the Sitemap: line
  in robots.txt all have to name the same host — a sitemap that advertises a
  different origin than the pages declare is the classic way to split a site in
  two and lose the ranking of both halves.

  No <lastmod> and no <priority>/<changefreq>: the dates would be guesses that
  rot the moment a page is edited, and search engines ignore the other two.
  Add a <lastmod> date here when a release actually changes a page.
-->
